IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-duties`
IMPORT `whs-qa`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (whs-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role
-- and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the situation does not
-- hold (FALSE, or `none of these`) and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. The two
-- enumerated situations are read through helpers that list every value with no OTHERWISE, so the trap of graffiti
-- finding 31 cannot hide a read of them.
--
-- For the worker (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the text
-- (most taken from the baseline's own cases, whs-cases-duties.l4, with the lives' event ids), and once against the
-- baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the business and the
-- officer, the values are worked by hand from the text. Facts the lives do not state are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked person` IS A `The other person`
ASSUME `an unasked control` IS A `Control of the place`
ASSUME `an unasked position` IS AN `Officer status`
ASSUME `an unasked duty holder` IS A `Duty holder`
ASSUME `an unasked outcome` IS A `What the failure did`
ASSUME `an unasked injury` IS A `My injury or illness`
ASSUME `an unasked exposure` IS AN `Exposure`
ASSUME `an unasked action` IS AN `Action at the site`
ASSUME `an unasked act` IS A `What was done to me`
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A `Why it was done`
ASSUME `an unasked proceeding` IS AN `Another proceeding`
ASSUME `an unasked act of mine` IS A `What I did to the worker`
ASSUME `an unasked reason of mine` IS A `Why I did it`

`as a worker` MEANS `I work for a business or undertaking`
`as the business` MEANS `I run a business or undertaking`
`as an officer` MEANS `I am a director or other officer of a business or undertaking`

-- The baseline's fixtures (whs-cases-duties.l4), with the same facts.

`Sentinel Security Services, the employer` MEANS `The other person` WITH
    `carries on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS TRUE
    `is an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer` IS FALSE
    `is a local government member` IS FALSE
    `is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes` IS FALSE
    `any of the volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group` IS FALSE

`Jarrah Legal Technologies, the tenant` MEANS `The other person` WITH
    `carries on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS TRUE
    `is an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer` IS FALSE
    `is a local government member` IS FALSE
    `is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes` IS FALSE
    `any of the volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group` IS FALSE

`the tower's building manager` MEANS `The other person` WITH
    `carries on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS TRUE
    `is an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer` IS FALSE
    `is a local government member` IS FALSE
    `is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes` IS FALSE
    `any of the volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group` IS FALSE

`a volunteer group that employs no one` MEANS `The other person` WITH
    `carries on a business or undertaking, alone or with others, for profit or not` IS TRUE
    `is an individual engaged in it solely as a worker or officer` IS FALSE
    `is a local government member` IS FALSE
    `is a group of volunteers working together for community purposes` IS TRUE
    `any of the volunteers employs a person to carry out work for the group` IS FALSE

`the tenant controls the stairwell under its lease` MEANS `Control of the place` WITH
    `its business involves management or control of the place, in whole or in part` IS TRUE
    `the place is a residence it occupies` IS FALSE
    `the residence is occupied for the purposes of a business or undertaking` IS FALSE
    `it is a prescribed person` IS FALSE

`no control of the stairwell` MEANS `Control of the place` WITH
    `its business involves management or control of the place, in whole or in part` IS FALSE
    `the place is a residence it occupies` IS FALSE
    `the residence is occupied for the purposes of a business or undertaking` IS FALSE
    `it is a prescribed person` IS FALSE

`the manager controls the common areas` MEANS `Control of the place` WITH
    `its business involves management or control of the place, in whole or in part` IS TRUE
    `the place is a residence it occupies` IS FALSE
    `the residence is occupied for the purposes of a business or undertaking` IS FALSE
    `it is a prescribed person` IS FALSE

`a householder's own home` MEANS `Control of the place` WITH
    `its business involves management or control of the place, in whole or in part` IS TRUE
    `the place is a residence it occupies` IS TRUE
    `the residence is occupied for the purposes of a business or undertaking` IS FALSE
    `it is a prescribed person` IS FALSE

`a fall on the stair, off eleven weeks on a doctor's certificate` MEANS `My injury or illness` WITH
    `needs immediate treatment as a hospital inpatient` IS FALSE
    `needs immediate treatment for` IS `none of the listed treatments`
    `needs a medical practitioner's treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance` IS FALSE
    `occurred in a remote location and needs urgent transfer to a medical facility` IS FALSE
    `a medical practitioner thinks it likely to keep me from my normal work for 10 days or more` IS TRUE
    `is a regulation 699 condition` IS `none of the regulation 699 conditions`
    `was contracted in work handling or in contact with animals or animal products` IS FALSE

`the same fall, with no doctor's opinion of 10 days off` MEANS `My injury or illness` WITH
    `needs immediate treatment as a hospital inpatient` IS FALSE
    `needs immediate treatment for` IS `none of the listed treatments`
    `needs a medical practitioner's treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance` IS FALSE
    `occurred in a remote location and needs urgent transfer to a medical facility` IS FALSE
    `a medical practitioner thinks it likely to keep me from my normal work for 10 days or more` IS FALSE
    `is a regulation 699 condition` IS `none of the regulation 699 conditions`
    `was contracted in work handling or in contact with animals or animal products` IS FALSE

